.Nd Distributed Hash Table (DHT) implementation for BitTorrent.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/dht.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_dht_new "struct mbt_dht **out" "struct mbt_ev *ev" "uint16_t port"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_dht_free "struct mbt_dht *d"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_dht_bootstrap "struct mbt_dht *d" "const char *addr" "uint16_t port"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_dht_get_peers "struct mbt_dht *d" "struct mbt_infohash *ih" "mbt_dht_peers_cb peers_cb" "mbt_dht_done_cb done_cb" "void *arg"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_dht_announce "struct mbt_dht *d" "struct mbt_infohash *ih" "uint16_t listen_port"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_dht_node_count "struct mbt_dht *d"
.Ft uint16_t
.Fn mbt_dht_port "struct mbt_dht *d"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_dht_set_node_id "struct mbt_dht *d" "const uint8_t id[20]"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_dht_set_verify "struct mbt_dht *d" "mbt_dht_verify_cb cb" "void *arg"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_dht_get_immutable "struct mbt_dht *d" "const uint8_t target[20]" "mbt_dht_item_cb cb" "void *arg"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_dht_put_immutable "struct mbt_dht *d" "const void *v" "size_t vlen" "mbt_dht_done_cb done_cb" "void *arg"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_dht_get_mutable "struct mbt_dht *d" "const uint8_t k[32]" "const char *salt" "size_t salt_len"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_dht_put_mutable "struct mbt_dht *d" "const uint8_t k[32]" "const uint8_t sig[64]" "int64_t seq" "const char *salt" "size_t salt_len" "const void *v" "size_t vlen" "mbt_dht_done_cb done_cb" "void *arg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn mbt_dht_set_peer_ttl
sets how long an announce from another node lasts, by default two hours.
A node keeps 8 peers for each infohash, and the oldest give way.
Announce again each hour.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_dht_set_max_stored
sets how many infohashes the node stores, by default 64.
Each takes about 300 bytes.
It returns 0 or a negative errno.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_dht_query
sends a raw KRPC query to an IP literal, for tests and tools.
.Fa args
is the
.Dq a
dictionary, sent as it is.
.Fa cb
gets the whole reply, which can be an error message, and is valid only during
the call.
It gets
.Er ETIMEDOUT
after 5 seconds, and
.Er ECANCELED
from
.Fn mbt_dht_free .
Errors are negative.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_dht_send_raw
sends bytes as they are.
.Fn mbt_dht_node_id
returns our 20 byte node id.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_dht_foreach_node
calls
.Fa cb
with the id, address and port of each node in the routing table.
.Fa cb
must not call into the DHT.
.Pp
The
.Nm mbt_dht
module provides a BitTorrent DHT implementation, supporting standard node operations and the server side of BEP 44
(arbitrary data storage).
The node stores items and answers get and put from other nodes.
It has no client that sends get or put over the network.
.Sh PEER DISCOVERY AND ANNOUNCEMENT
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It Fn mbt_dht_bootstrap
Sends a find_node request to a known node to populate the local routing table.
.It Fn mbt_dht_get_peers
Searches the DHT for peers associated with the given infohash.
.It Fn mbt_dht_announce
Announces the caller's presence as a peer for the specified infohash.
Returns the number of nodes told, or -EINVAL with no prior get_peers.
.El
.Sh DATA STORAGE (BEP 44)
These calls use the local store, which serves other nodes.
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It Fn mbt_dht_get_item
Reads a stored item of either kind.
.It Fn mbt_dht_immutable_target
Computes the key of an immutable item from its bencoded value.
.It Fn mbt_dht_mutable_target
Computes the key of a mutable item from its public key and salt.
.It Fn mbt_dht_get_immutable
Retrieves an immutable item from the DHT using its SHA-1 hash.
.It Fn mbt_dht_put_immutable
Stores an immutable item. The key is derived from the value's SHA-1 hash.
.It Fn mbt_dht_get_mutable
Retrieves a mutable item using its public key and optional salt.
.It Fn mbt_dht_put_mutable
Stores a mutable item with key, signature, sequence number, and value.
.El
